      "countAsQuest:1": 1,
      "desc:8": "§6Chlorocalcite§r comes out of bedrock ore processing and is a source of §6Calcium§r and §bChlorine§r.\n\n1. §3Industrial Mixer§r: chlorocalcite, water and nitric acid make §bChlorocalcite Solution§r.\n2. §3Industrial Mixer§r: the solution, sulfuric acid and flux make §bMixed Chlorocalcite Solution§r.\n3. §3Fractioning Tower§r: it separates into §bCleaned Chlorocalcite Solution§r and colloid.\n4. §3Chemical Plant§r: with plenty of sulfuric acid it splits into §bPotassium Chloride§r and §bCalcium Chloride§r solutions.\n5. §3Electrolysis Machine§r: both give chlorine, and calcium chloride also leaves §bCalcium Solution§r.\n6. §3Coker Unit§r: calcium solution becomes calcium powder.\n\nFor a quick bit of calcium, a Combination Oven turns chlorocalcite into calcium powder and chlorine directly.",
